Chapter: FsLayer
  cites Foreword chapter FileSystem
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16

 The FileSystem layer: a handler services the FileSystem
 effect's ops over the disk, and the program above it never touches the
 disk at all.

 app-body is the program. Its row says FileSystem.Read and
 FileSystem.Write and nothing else -- it performs read-text and
 write-file as bare effect ops and could not name a sector if it wanted
 to. serve-files is the layer. Its row says Device.Block and nothing
 else: the `with FileSystem` handler discharges the app's whole family
 by the dotted lattice (rung 1), and each clause services its op with a
 fat16 call, whose Device.Block is what the clause bodies re-emit into
 the layer's own row. That is the attenuation this test exists to pin:
 the authority to touch the disk lives in the layer, the app carries
 only the FileSystem grant, and neither signature could absorb the
 other's without the def boundary rejecting it.

 The runtime half is a real round trip: the app writes NOTE.TXT through
 the handler, reads it back through the handler, and the bytes must
 match. The absent path answers through the same handler, so a wrong
 dispatch cannot hide -- a read that went to the serial port instead of
 the disk (the read-file builtin trap this op exists to avoid) would
 hang or answer garbage, never "<absent>".

Section: Layer

  fsl-read-vol : Fat16Volume, Text -> [Device.Block] Text
  fsl-read-vol (vol) (p) = when fat16-read-text vol p
    is Just (t) -> t
    is None -> "<absent>"

  fsl-read : Text -> [Device.Block] Text
  fsl-read (p) = act
    vol <- fat16-boot-volume
    fsl-read-vol vol p
  end

  serve-files : Integer -> [Device.Block] Text
  serve-files (x) = act
    with FileSystem (app-body x)
      read-text (p) (resume) = resume (fsl-read p)
      write-file (p) (c) (resume) = resume (fat16-write-file p c)
  end

Section: App

  app-body : Integer -> [FileSystem.Read, FileSystem.Write] Text
  app-body (x) =
    if x == 0 then
      (if write-file "NOTE.TXT" "from the layer" then read-text "NOTE.TXT" else "<write failed>")
    else read-text "NOPE.XXX"

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Block] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("layer " & serve-files 0)
    print-line-uni ("absent " & serve-files 1)
  end
